# Method name, software identifier or literal command intentionally preserved.
#: README.md:1
msgid "VMetaD-tutorial"
msgstr "VMetaD-tutorial"

#: README.md:2
msgid ""
"A tutorial to setup and run Volume-based Metadynamics simulations. The "
"original work which explains the theory for Volume-based Metadynamics "
"(VMetaD) is [this](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jpclett.9b01183). Some time "
"later, in [this](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.1c00649) paper we added "
"some details (the RMSD restraining) which we will use in this tutorial."
msgstr ""
"Volume-based Metadynamics の設定・実行を学ぶ Tutorial です。Volume-based Metadynamics "
"(VMetaD) の理論は [原著](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jpclett.9b01183) "
"で説明しています。その後の [論文](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.1c00649) で加えた RMSD "
"Restraint も、ここで使います。"

#: README.md:4
msgid "This guide is divided in different sections"
msgstr "このガイドは、複数のセクションに分かれている。"

#: README.md:6
msgid "Volume-based Metadynamics theory"
msgstr "Volume-based Metadynamics の理論"

#: README.md:7
msgid "A brief introduction to the rationale behind the use of VMetaD."
msgstr "VMetaD を用いる考え方の簡単な入門。"

#: README.md:9
msgid "Case study: L99A T4 Lysozyme:Benzene"
msgstr "適用事例：L99A T4 Lysozyme:Benzene"

#: README.md:10
msgid ""
"We will present the case study for this tutorial, a small engineered protein"
" which binds benzene. We will use, to favor the possibility to test the "
"method without that need of HPC resources, a simplified model called multi-"
"eGO (more details [here](https://doi.org/10.26434/chemrxiv-2024-jcmgc)) "
"which can run on laptop/workstation at the timescales of interest."
msgstr ""
"Benzene と結合する小さな改変タンパク質を例に使います。HPC を必要とせず試せるよう、Laptop/Workstation "
"で対象の時間スケールを計算できる簡略モデル multi-eGO を使います（詳細は "
"[こちら](https://doi.org/10.26434/chemrxiv-2024-jcmgc)）。"

#: README.md:12
msgid "Input files preparation"
msgstr "入力ファイルの準備"

#: README.md:13
msgid ""
"We will discuss all the preliminary steps to set up VMetaD, from the "
"restraining potential size to the selection of the atoms that define the "
"reference frame. We will also discuss all the PLUMED instructions to "
"implement the method."
msgstr ""
"Restraint Potential の大きさから参照座標系を定める原子の選択まで、VMetaD の準備を説明します。実装に必要な PLUMED "
"の全指示も扱います。"

#: README.md:15
msgid "Post-processing, reweighting and entropic correction"
msgstr "後処理、Reweighting、Entropic Correction"

#: README.md:16
msgid ""
"Finally, we will discuss how to analyze the VMetaD files to get the binding "
"free energy difference, reweighting the free energy surface on apt CVs. We "
"will also discuss how to compute the entropic correction due to the presence"
" of the restraining potential."
msgstr ""
"最後に、適切な CV に自由エネルギー表面を Reweighting し、VMetaD の出力から結合自由エネルギー差を求めます。Restraint "
"Potential による Entropy 補正の計算法も説明します。"

#: README.md:18
msgid ""
"___NB:___ This tutorial assumes that you know metadynamics theory and "
"practice in PLUMED (if not, a good start can be the [PLUMED "
"tutorial](https://www.plumed-"
"tutorials.org/lessons/21/004/data/NAVIGATION.html) about it)."
msgstr ""
"___注：___ PLUMED の Metadynamics の理論と実践を知っていることを前提とします。未習の場合は [PLUMED "
"Tutorial](https://www.plumed-"
"tutorials.org/lessons/21/004/data/NAVIGATION.html) から始めるとよいでしょう。"
